{"metadata":{"citation_count_without_self_citations":7,"citation_count":7,"publication_info":[{"year":2025,"page_end":"2465","page_start":"2355","journal_issue":"7","journal_title":"Annales Henri Poincare","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1212474"},"journal_volume":"26"}],"dois":[{"value":"10.1007/s00023-024-01489-0","source":"Springer"}],"titles":[{"title":"A Construction of Approximately Self-Similar Naked Singularities for the Spherically Symmetric Einstein-Scalar Field System","source":"Springer"},{"title":"A construction of approximately self-similar naked singularities for the spherically symmetric Einstein-scalar field system","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"ids":[{"value":"0009-0000-2100-982X","schema":"ORCID"}],"uuid":"b5028372-e6a1-445c-933d-cdfc4b30d1d7","emails":["jaydeeps@math.princeton.edu"],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1959996"},"full_name":"Singh, Jaydeep","signature_block":"SANGHj","raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Mathematics, Princeton University, Washington Road, 08544 Princeton, NJ, USA"}],"affiliations_identifiers":[{"value":"grid.16750.35","schema":"GRID"}]}],"curated":false,"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint"}],"texkeys":["Singh:2022uyx"],"citeable":true,"imprints":[{"date":"2024-09-27"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"In this work, we identify stable perturbations of k-self-similar naked singularities, in the full parameter range $k^2 \\in (0, \\frac{1}{3}).$ As a consequence, we provide a dynamical construction of naked singularity interior and exterior regions outside of exact self-similarity, extending the work of Chrisotodoulou (Ann Math 140:607–653, 1994). More generally, we consider a wide range of singular spacetimes satisfying self-similar bounds, and parameterize perturbations in terms of fine-tuned data for the scalar field along the past lightcone of the singularity. This data is required to satisfy conditions consistent with the absence of a blue-shift instability and is therefore non-generic. The argument combines a backwards stability argument in the interior region with a global existence problem in the exterior region, adapting techniques developed by Rodnianski and Shlapentokh-Rothman (Naked singularities for the Einstein vacuum equations: the exterior solution. arXiv:1912.08478. 2019) to the spherically symmetric setting.","source":"Springer"},{"value":"In this work we investigate the stability and instability properties of a class of naked singularity spacetimes. The first rigorous study of naked singularity formation in the spherically symmetric Einstein-scalar field system was due to Christodoulou, who constructed a family $(\\overline{g}_k, \\overline{\\phi}_k)$ of $k$-self-similar solutions, for any $k^2 \\in (0,\\frac{1}{3})$. We extend the construction to produce examples of interior and exterior regions of naked singularity spacetimes locally modeled on the $(\\overline{g}_k, \\overline{\\phi}_k)$, without requiring exact self-similarity. The main result is a global stability statement under fine-tuned data perturbations, for a class of naked singularity spacetimes satisfying self-similar bounds. Given the well-known blueshift instability for suitably regular naked singularities in the Einstein-scalar field model, we require non-generic conditions on the data perturbations. In particular, the scalar field perturbation along the past lightcone of the singular point $\\mathcal{O}$ vanishes to high order near $\\mathcal{O}$. Technical difficulties arise from the singular behavior of the background solution, as well as regularity considerations at the axis and past lightcone of the singularity. The interior region is constructed via a backwards stability argument, thereby avoiding activating the blueshift instability. The extension to the exterior region is treated as a global existence problem to the future of $\\mathcal{O}$, adapting techniques of Rodnianski and Shlapentokh-Rothman for vacuum spacetimes.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1789450"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[1] , Alexakis, S., Fournodavlos, G.: Stable space-like singularity formation for axi-symmetric and polarized near-Schwarzschild black hole interiors. (2020). , http://arxiv.org/abs/2004.00692","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"2004.00692"}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1395073"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[2] X. An, X. Zhang, \"Examples of naked singularity formation in higher-dimensional Einstein-vacuum spacetimes\", Ann. Henri Poincar é,19,619, DOI: 10.1007/s00023-017-0631-9","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.1007/s00023-017-0631-9"],"label":"2","title":{"title":"Examples of naked singularity formation in higher-dimensional Einstein-vacuum spacetimes"},"authors":[{"full_name":"An, X."},{"full_name":"Zhang, X."}],"publication_info":{"year":2017,"artid":"619","page_start":"619","journal_title":"Ann. Henri Poincar é","journal_volume":"19"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/33714"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[3] MW Choptuik, \"Universality and scaling in gravitational collapse of a massless scalar field\", Phys.Rev.Lett.,70,9-12, DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.70.9","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevLett.70.9"],"label":"3","title":{"title":"Universality and scaling in gravitational collapse of a massless scalar field"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Choptuik, MW"}],"publication_info":{"year":1993,"page_end":"12","page_start":"9","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214495"},"journal_volume":"70"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/211917"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[4] D. Christodoulou, \"Violation of cosmic censorship in the gravitational collapse of a dust cloud\", Commun.Math.Phys.,93,171-195, DOI: 10.1007/BF01223743","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.1007/BF01223743"],"label":"4","title":{"title":"Violation of cosmic censorship in the gravitational collapse of a dust cloud"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."}],"publication_info":{"year":1984,"page_end":"195","page_start":"171","journal_title":"Commun.Math.Phys.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214791"},"journal_volume":"93"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1235882"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[5] D. Christodoulou, \"The formation of black holes and singularities in spherically symmetric gravitational collapse\", Commun.Pure Appl.Math.,44,339-373, DOI: 10.1002/cpa.3160440305","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.1002/cpa.3160440305"],"label":"5","title":{"title":"The formation of black holes and singularities in spherically symmetric gravitational collapse"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."}],"publication_info":{"year":1991,"page_end":"373","page_start":"339","journal_title":"Commun.Pure Appl.Math.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214782"},"journal_volume":"44"}}},{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[6] D. Christodoulou, \"Bounded variation solutions of the spherically symmetric Einstein-scalar field equations\", Commun.Pure Appl.Math.,46,1131-1220, DOI: 10.1002/cpa.3160460803","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.1002/cpa.3160460803"],"label":"6","title":{"title":"Bounded variation solutions of the spherically symmetric Einstein-scalar field equations"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."}],"publication_info":{"year":1993,"page_end":"1220","page_start":"1131","journal_title":"Commun.Pure Appl.Math.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214782"},"journal_volume":"46"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/391017"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[7] D. Christodoulou, \"Examples of naked singularity formation in the gravitational collapse of a scalar field\", Annals Math.,140,607-653, DOI: 10.2307/2118619","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.2307/2118619"],"label":"7","title":{"title":"Examples of naked singularity formation in the gravitational collapse of a scalar field"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."}],"publication_info":{"year":1994,"page_end":"653","page_start":"607","journal_title":"Annals Math.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214864"},"journal_volume":"140"}}},{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[8] D. Christodoulou, \"On the global initial value problem and the issue of singularities\", Class. Quant. Grav.,16,A23, DOI: 10.1088/0264-9381/16/12A/302","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.1088/0264-9381/16/12A/302"],"label":"8","title":{"title":"On the global initial value problem and the issue of singularities"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."}],"publication_info":{"year":1999,"artid":"A23","page_start":"A23","journal_title":"Class.Quant.Grav.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214779"},"journal_volume":"16"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2946377"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[9] D. Christodoulou, \"The instability of naked singularities in the gravitational collapse of a scalar field\", Annals Math.,149,183-217, DOI: 10.2307/121023","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"dois":["10.2307/121023"],"label":"9","title":{"title":"The instability of naked singularities in the gravitational collapse of a scalar field"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."}],"publication_info":{"year":1999,"page_end":"217","page_start":"183","journal_title":"Annals Math.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214864"},"journal_volume":"149"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2151069"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[10] , Cicortas, S.: Extensions of Lorentzian Hawking-Page solutions with null singularities, spacelike singularit